<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,619,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,619,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 11/27/96    11/20/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,619,000  29,683,000    28,228,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 124,930     133,818	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   11/27/96    11/20/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,472,000   5,289,000     4,801,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,944,000   5,025,000     4,504,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,060,000   4,837,000     5,062,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,126,000   3,178,000     2,885,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,227,000   4,017,000     3,849,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,547,000   5,346,000     5,118,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,244,000   1,991,000     2,009,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,619,000  29,683,000    28,228,000</p>
</text>
